Modern Bag — TM/HM machine labels clip past the right edge of the item window

Upstream: FAFF0x/gen1recomp, modern_bag 1.6.0 (modern_bag_v1.6.0.zip)
Target:   modern_bag/main.lua, compactMachineLabel (line 294 in 1.6.0)

compactMachineLabel budgets the label at 15 characters, which is wider than the
row actually shows. A 15-character label such as "TM01 MEGA PUNCH" therefore
fails the "#label > maxChars" test, is never truncated, and draws past the right
border. A 17-character label is cut to 14 characters plus ".", still 15, so the
ellipsis lands outside the window and the truncation is invisible.

13 is the widest budget that stops the overflow. The marked branch keeps the
same 4-character gap below the unmarked budget that 1.6.0 already used, so
marker behaviour is unchanged.

Verified with Lua 5.4:
  - applies clean to stock modern_bag_v1.6.0.zip with "patch -p1"
  - patched main.lua passes "luac5.4 -p"
  - both shipped test files pass before and after, unmodified:
      lua5.4 tests/modern_bag_test.lua
      lua5.4 tests/modern_ui_compat_test.lua
NOT verified on-device.

Known wart: at width 13 "TM03 SWORDS DANCE" renders "TM03 SWORDS ." — the cut
lands on a space, so the period floats. Left alone; it is a separate change.

Apply from the unpacked mod's parent directory with: patch -p1 < this file

--- a/modern_bag/main.lua
+++ b/modern_bag/main.lua
@@ -291,8 +291,19 @@
   }
 end
 
+-- Machine rows are budgeted by character count. The item window fits fewer
+-- glyphs than the previous budget of 15 assumed, so 15-character labels such
+-- as "TM01 MEGA PUNCH" never reached the truncation branch below and drew
+-- past the right border. 13 is the widest budget that stops the overflow in
+-- the TM/HM pocket; the marked variant keeps the original 4-character gap
+-- reserved for the "P"/"F"/"PF" row markers.
+-- Lower these if your display still clips.
+local MACHINE_LABEL_WIDTH = 13
+local MACHINE_LABEL_WIDTH_MARKED = 9
+
 local function compactMachineLabel(info, markers)
-  local maxChars = markers ~= "" and 11 or 15
+  local maxChars = markers ~= "" and MACHINE_LABEL_WIDTH_MARKED
+    or MACHINE_LABEL_WIDTH
   local label = info.code .. " " .. info.name
   if #label > maxChars then label = label:sub(1, maxChars - 1) .. "." end
   return label
